WEBVTT

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.950
It's still raining.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.590
The weather forecast said
the rainy season would end today.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.010
I didn't bring an umbrella!

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.380
Hey, Nishikata!

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.710
What is it, Takagi-san?

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.610
What's wrong?

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.150
Nothing.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:56.070
Ah, it's raining.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.600
I'm glad I brought a 
folding umbrella just in case.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.900
Nishikata, did you bring an umbrella?

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.460
Eh, umm...

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.790
Hmm, you didn't bring one!

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:14.580
It's fine. It will probably 
stop in the afternoon.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.510
What if it won't stop?

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:19.470
In this case...

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.930
In this case?

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:39.120
Wait, Takagi-san!

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.450
You're too close!

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:43.660
Nishikata!

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:45.980
What might this be?

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.670
This is...

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.880
...a lover's umbrella!

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:59.240
Takagi-san, are you inviting me
to share an umbrella?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.640
What should I do?

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.960
As I'm aiming for a perfect
attendance award...

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.380
...I want to avoid getting wet
and risk catching a cold!

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.860
Maybe I should just accept.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:20.520
Takagi-san, that umbrella...

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.120
The answer is:
A fish bone!

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.540
Huh? Nishikata?
What did you think it was?

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.880
The rain has stopped.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.320
How disappointing...

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:01.850
I wanted to share an umbrella
with you again, Nishikata.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.290
After all, you were just teasing me...

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.690
...with the shared umbrella, weren't you?

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.780
That’s a relief.
The sky cleared up.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.990
You said you wanted to have a contest,
even if it takes a detour on our way home.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.760
We can't play <i>Guriko</i>
while sharing an umbrella, right?

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.470
Yeah.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:30.170
Then... Let's go home together...

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:30.940
Yeah!

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.380
Nishikata!

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:39.090
Summer is beginning.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:50.410
Teasing Master Takagi-san:
 The Movie

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:50.410
Subtitles by RNEsub

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:27.030
<i>♪ Passing through the short shadows, ♪
♪ a flock of cheerful birds. ♪</i>

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:36.030
<i>♪ Chasing and overtaking, just like us. ♪</i>

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.800
<i>♪ As if to announce that summer is here. ♪</i>

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.040
<i>♪ The waves shine and light up the sky ♪</i>

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:54.710
<i>♪ Even on ordinary days, ♪
♪ they sparkle brightly. ♪</i>

00:04:56.590 --> 00:05:05.260
<i>♪ Under the sun where we ♪
♪ exchanged countless promises. ♪</i>

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:10.080
<i>♪ A bright and unseen tomorrow. ♪</i>

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.230
<i>♪ Summer is still beginning. ♪</i>

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:18.690
<i>♪ May it continue. ♪</i>

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:23.620
<i>♪ Summer is still beginning. ♪</i>

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.940
CHI YO KO RE I TO
(Chocolate)

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.940
Rock! Paper! Scissors!

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.320
GU RI KO
(Glico)

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.170
One more win and it's a goal!

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:08.260
Same here, Takagi-san!

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:13.870
But I didn't expect you
to only use scissors so far.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.220
Hehehe...

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:20.310
What do you think, Takagi-san?
This is my superb strategy!

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:25.550
You can only beat scissors with
rock, which has a low number of steps.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:29.220
Takagi-san has three steps.
I have six!

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:33.410
It's sufficient if I win
one out of three.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.520
Takagi-san would have won,
if she kept using rock.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.710
But actually...

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:43.700
The uncertainty that I
might use paper or rock.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.590
You're at my mercy!

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.450
I feel sorry for you, Takagi-san!

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:55.540
This advanced psychological tactic
must have worn your nerves down!

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.140
Thanks to you,
it was easy to adjust.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.270
Naa?!

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.090
Hey, anyway, the match will be
decided in one more round!

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:04.170
Have we decided
for a punishment?

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.970
Ah... right...

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:11.820
Easy to adjust?
Heh, sore loser...

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:15.730
There is no point
in sticking to my plan.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:19.150
Sore loser!

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.670
So... The person who loses by 
using paper must buy drinks.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:26.910
The person who loses by using rock
will get a forehead-flick. Okay?

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:30.450
Okay! And...

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.880
...what if anyone loses with scissors?

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.850
A kiss!

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.590
So, let's start!

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.270
Rock! Paper!...
Wait!

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.920
What should I do?

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.860
If I use the scissors here...

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.950
...doesn't it sound like
I want to kiss her?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:54.100
No, but I've been sticking
to scissors so far.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:58.730
I don't want to use anything else now.
But... But...

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:02.460
Craaap!

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:06.030
Ah! Did I win?

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:09.950
CHI YO KO RE I TO
(Chocolate)

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:11.760
What a pity!

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:15.160
Now I understand...

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:19.520
I thought I had a good game going.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.380
I was played with...

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:24.880
...from the start.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.680
Shall we go buy some drinks?

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:29.110
Yes...

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.290
Here you go!
-Thank you!

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:44.750
Damn you, Takagi-san!

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:49.460
Let's do it again!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.740
Yeah.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:53.800
The next time...

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.890
Next time, if anyone wins 
with scissors, let's make it a kiss rule!

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.970
Damn you, Takagi-san!

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:18.060
I was teased three times
that day by Takagi-san.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:20.490
I was teased a lot today, too.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.900
Moreover, I recently started
'teasing savings'.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.790
It's putting pressure on my finances.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.330
But!

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:33.280
This is my punishment for being
teased by Takagi-san so much.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:38.160
I need to raise my awareness
to win next time.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.300
Gyaoon!

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:45.210
My dinosaur piggy bank is 
telling me to do my best.

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:52.320
Next time, if anyone wins 
with scissors, let's make it a kiss rule!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:58.010
Thi... This counts as memory teasing!

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.060
Three more push-ups!

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:03.190
One! Two!

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:06.860
Three!

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:16.170
Good! Look at the camera for the next one.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.260
Like this?

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.830
Ohh! That's it! That's it!

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:24.120
What are you doing in my seat?

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.290
We are members
of the graduating committee.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:30.000
So we are taking pictures
of daily life in class.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.300
Yes! My daily life at your desk, Nakai.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.140
Nishikata, Nakai! Look at this, too!

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:44.370
Eh, who's that?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.370
That's me. Me.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.770
Takao fixed it up with an app.

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:50.020
It looks nothing like you.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:53.280
Hey, look at the others, too!

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.900
Look! Look!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.120
Geez​...

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.870
Where is the daily life
scene supposed to be?

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.870
What happened to me?

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:06.220
Looks like a ghost photo.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.940
We will cut you out later.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.180
No, no, Nishikata! 
As an apology, I'll make it look good!

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:16.630
That's not allowed!

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.570
Takao! Kimura!
Listen up!

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:26.230
The pictures you take will remain
in the graduation album forever.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.560
This time will never come again.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.900
I want you to record it so that you
can look back on it in the future.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.340
That's the duty of a
graduate committee member!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.990
Take this seriously!

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.740
Yes, we are sorry.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.790
Not fair, wait!

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:46.970
Don't run there.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:50.500
Nishikata!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.920
Nishikata?

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:00.690
Ah! What is it? Takagi-san.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:04.470
I wondered why
you looked zoned out.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:06.660
I'm not...

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.440
Hmm?

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.360
No, it's more like...

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:18.530
Takagi-san, you want to have contest?

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:20.420
Sounds good. What kind?

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.910
A breath-holding contest!

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.180
The rules are simple!

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:32.090
The one who can stay 
underwater longer, wins.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.140
Sounds good!

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:36.970
Good! To tell you the truth...

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:41.300
I've been secretly practicing
for this contest!

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:48.740
I'll dive first.
Takagi-san, you count!

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:52.650
I'll count when it's your turn.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:56.190
But that might not be
a good idea for a contest.

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:57.190
What?

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:59.900
So, while the other person is underwater...

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:03.530
...and you count slower,
you will win, right?

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:04.740
Oh...

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.040
That's why we should
dive at the same time.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.830
You will lose if your
face is above water first.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.810
I get it...

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:18.420
By the way,
one more thing...

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.970
Don't make funny faces 
underwater to make me laugh!

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:24.400
Okay!

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.960
Alright. Now there's no back door.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:33.830
I won't let Takagi-san tease me
for three years of middle school in a row.

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:37.690
Starting today, I will win!

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:39.880
Alright!

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:41.900
One! Two! Three!

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:38.190
SU KI
(I like you.)

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:56.060
Nishikata, are you okay?

00:14:56.060 --> 00:15:00.150
It's because you said
something strange.

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.650
Something strange?

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:05.490
Umm, well...

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:11.340
I was almost out of breath.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:15.460
So I was trying to say
that I was about to return to the surface.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:16.640
Wha...?

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.230
Did you misunderstand something?

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:23.840
No... Not at all.

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.050
So, it's my win?

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.340
Yeah.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.720
Okay, it's time!
Everybody get out!

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:38.520
This is the last year at the pool.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.370
High schools have pools, too.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:43.440
Yes, but it's a different a pool.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:48.280
The pool at the high school
is much bigger, isn't it?

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.780
It's much deeper, isn't it?

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:53.790
Stop it, Mina!
I don't want to hear this.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.470
What if you could swim just fine?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.420
I wouldn't struggle if I could.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:02.710
I want to go to a high school
without a pool.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:04.560
Is there such a place?

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:08.650
Most likely somewhere... But...

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:13.570
I'm going to go to high school
here on the island with everybody else.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:17.030
So we are together every day.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:24.920
Yukari-chan! Sanae-chan!

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:28.630
Let's be friends
together and forever!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:29.710
Hmm?

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.590
It's inevitable.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.160
Yukari-chan!
-What?

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.560
Yukari-chan!
-What?

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:47.560
Mano-chan!

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:49.550
Wha... What?

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:52.010
Did something good happen?

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:54.280
It's written on your face.

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:57.240
Yes.

00:16:57.770 --> 00:17:00.700
Do you know that rumour?

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.520
About the fireflies.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.780
Come on man, cheer up!

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.550
You sigh every five seconds.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.450
What's the matter?

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.750
Nishikata!

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.680
Nishikata, listen!

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:27.380
I asked Hojo to go to the beach
with me on summer vacation.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.920
And then...

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:30.300
Impossible!
-Eh?

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.550
Right.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.140
I'll be in Canada for the summer.

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:36.560
What?

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.120
I'm visiting a summer school.
That's why it's not possible.

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:44.580
Is there such a thing?
It's the last summer of middle school.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:53.010
That's amazing. I've only been
to a few places off the island.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:56.720
Over there, they are
proactive when it comes to love.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:01.660
Hi! What's your name?
-I'm Hojo! ♥

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.890
Oh, I love you! Come on!

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.420
Oh, yes! Kiss! Kikikiss! ♥

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:09.260
Stop it!

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:10.510
This is a serious matter!

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:12.550
Calm down, Hamaguchi!

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:14.640
But it has a good side, too.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.110
Ah, that's right!

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:20.100
Hojo will go shopping at the end of the
week to prepare for summer school.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:21.580
She asked me
if I would like to come.

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.910
Well, I'll help her carry stuff.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.000
That's good, isn't it?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.190
Oh no!

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:34.710
That day I have community work.
I was supposed to help scare off bugs.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.830
I'd like to take over for you.

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:43.140
But I'm going to a barbecue
restaurant with my family. Sorry.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:46.850
I have an online game event
coming up. Sorry.

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:50.480
Nishikata, are you free this Saturday?

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.130
No problem,
I don't have anything special to do.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:58.530
Nishikata! Thanks!
My summer ends on this one day.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:02.730
You and Takagi-san will have the last
summer in middle school. Cherish it!

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:04.580
What are you...?

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.790
On <i>White Day</i>,
you didn't end up confessing.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:14.170
I didn't...

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:26.810
Hey, Nishikata.
-Hey, Takagi-san.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:29.680
Takagi-san, you go first.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.590
Did you see fireflies this year?

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:37.110
Fireflies?

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:42.010
No, this year...
I haven't seen any in years.

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:44.270
When I was little, I used to go
see them with my parents.

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:46.700
Me too. How about
going out to see them again?

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.330
What do you mean?

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:52.290
I want to see them with you!

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.460
And you, Nishikata?

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.070
What were you trying to say just now?

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:04.660
What was it? I forgot..

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:06.540
Nishikata, your face is red.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:08.250
It's not particularly red.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:10.960
It's because of the setting sun.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.470
Gyaoon!

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.600
You and Takagi-san...

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:28.540
...will have the last
summer in middle school. Cherish it!

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.630
I want to see them with you!

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:48.120
On <i>White Day</i>,
you didn't end up confessing.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:50.290
I didn't...

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:52.890
Take her with you when you
scare off the bugs.

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:08.520
Do you know that rumour?

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:09.410
Hmm?

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:11.810
About the fireflies.

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:15.190
When you see fireflies
for the first time in the year...

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:18.670
...you will be forever united
with the person you love.

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:22.130
I may have heard of it.
-Did you go to see them with Nakai?

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:25.700
Yeah.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:31.200
And then,
he invited me to a movie I wanted to see.

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:36.710
Takagi-chan, you better go
see them with Nishikata, too!

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:38.590
Aren't you worried?

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:43.300
Even if we go to high school.
Will it be like this forever?

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.400
Takagi-san, let's scare off bugs together.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:59.400
We might even see fireflies.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.760
I sent it...

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:06.990
No... Takagi-san said
she wanted to see fireflies.

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:08.450
I just invited her...

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:11.100
But she might already have plans.

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:14.290
Ah, Takagi-san!

00:22:14.290 --> 00:22:16.020
Let's go!

00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:20.480
Let's go scare off bugs.
Together with you, Nishikata.

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:26.300
I invited you because you said
you wanted to see fireflies.

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:27.720
Yup!

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:30.070
There's no deeper meaning to it...

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:31.450
Yup!

00:22:32.060 --> 00:22:34.160
Are you maybe teasing me?

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:36.620
No. I'm really happy!

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:41.740
I'll get back to you about
the meeting time.

00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:42.960
Yup!

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:45.240
See you then.

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:47.830
See you then.

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:13.950
Thank you very much!

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:28.370
Let's go!

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:53.020
Tomose! Tomose!
(Burn! Burn!)

00:24:00.980 --> 00:24:02.500
There you go!

00:24:03.070 --> 00:24:04.940
Please take this!

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:07.780
Nooo, I wanna go home!

00:24:07.780 --> 00:24:11.160
Hey, what's wrong?

00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:13.160
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:24:13.160 --> 00:24:16.000
No, please wait a moment.

00:24:17.460 --> 00:24:19.210
Why don't you want to?

00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:24.760
I'm scared.

00:24:24.760 --> 00:24:28.940
Everyone said there would
be Yokai monsters.

00:24:28.940 --> 00:24:32.650
Yokai? You mean Kaboso?

00:24:34.810 --> 00:24:35.990
You know him?

00:24:35.990 --> 00:24:37.990
Yes, I know him!

00:24:38.600 --> 00:24:43.420
Kaboso will come out
when people gather at night...

00:24:43.420 --> 00:24:47.400
...and imitate human
voices and play pranks....

00:24:47.400 --> 00:24:49.990
...but in truth...

00:24:49.990 --> 00:24:52.950
...he's a good guy
with a kind side.

00:24:55.450 --> 00:24:59.670
But, but... he's so hairy.
His eyes are ghastly.

00:24:59.670 --> 00:25:02.890
His teeth are really sharp, aren't they?

00:25:02.890 --> 00:25:04.750
Grrr! Grrr!

00:25:06.090 --> 00:25:08.970
That's a bit dramatic.

00:25:08.970 --> 00:25:14.640
Oh, yes, that's right.
I'm friends with the Yokai.

00:25:14.640 --> 00:25:17.140
I'll tell him not to scare you.
Don't worry!

00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:20.290
Really?

00:25:20.290 --> 00:25:21.520
Yes!

00:25:22.690 --> 00:25:25.170
Pinky swear?

00:25:26.030 --> 00:25:26.620
Yes!

00:25:28.840 --> 00:25:36.220
♪ If you break the promise ♪
♪ swallow thousand needles. ♪

00:25:36.220 --> 00:25:40.140
And you will be stomped by an elephant!
And chased by a bear in the forest!

00:25:40.140 --> 00:25:42.100
And a tiger and a lion, too.

00:25:42.100 --> 00:25:43.810
Isn't that enough?

00:25:46.020 --> 00:25:48.270
Pinky promise!

00:25:49.210 --> 00:25:50.610
Bye Bye!

00:25:50.610 --> 00:25:52.570
Bye Bye!

00:25:55.640 --> 00:25:57.890
So that was it.

00:25:59.020 --> 00:26:00.370
I didn't know...

00:26:01.310 --> 00:26:03.080
...that you were friends with Yokai.

00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:05.310
Did you see that?

00:26:05.310 --> 00:26:07.670
This was because of the situation.

00:26:07.670 --> 00:26:09.500
But you were really cool.

00:26:09.500 --> 00:26:11.650
You looked like a father.

00:26:13.700 --> 00:26:15.240
A father?

00:26:22.290 --> 00:26:25.790
I can go home after saying goodbye,
so please wait for me.

00:26:25.790 --> 00:26:27.090
Yeah.

00:26:28.380 --> 00:26:29.900
Ah, Aoki-san!

00:26:29.900 --> 00:26:32.720
Hey!
-I'm done!

00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:35.550
Thank you for your help today!

00:26:41.020 --> 00:26:43.690
Your girlfriend?

00:26:43.690 --> 00:26:45.350
No, it's not like that!

00:26:45.350 --> 00:26:48.820
It's great to be young!

00:26:48.820 --> 00:26:51.500
Ten years ago, Grandma and I went
to a bug scare off.

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:55.950
That's why it's different!
We just wanted to see the fireflies!

00:26:55.950 --> 00:26:58.220
Fireflies?

00:26:58.220 --> 00:26:59.720
Hmm?

00:27:50.840 --> 00:27:52.190
It's beautiful.

00:27:53.420 --> 00:27:54.420
Yeah.

00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:05.480
Um, Takagi-san.

00:28:05.480 --> 00:28:06.600
Hmm?

00:28:06.600 --> 00:28:09.310
Why did you want to see fireflies?

00:28:11.650 --> 00:28:14.280
Because if you see them
your wish will come true.

00:28:14.280 --> 00:28:17.320
Like a shooting star?

00:28:19.570 --> 00:28:21.280
Something like that.

00:28:23.490 --> 00:28:26.120
I'm sorry, I just heard about this.

00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:31.770
Fireflies don't seem to be around anymore
by the time the bugs are scared off.

00:28:34.920 --> 00:28:35.900
Yeah.

00:28:35.900 --> 00:28:38.400
What? Did you know about this?

00:28:40.680 --> 00:28:42.180
Yes.

00:28:42.180 --> 00:28:46.640
But I thought I could find some
with you, Nishikata.

00:28:49.660 --> 00:28:54.540
I'll look on this side,
you look on the other side, Takagi-san.

00:29:23.180 --> 00:29:25.390
Thank you for today.

00:29:25.390 --> 00:29:28.100
Let's look for fireflies next year!

00:29:28.100 --> 00:29:29.030
Yeah.

00:29:30.390 --> 00:29:34.060
We'll be in high school then.

00:29:35.770 --> 00:29:37.960
I don't really feel like it.

00:29:39.030 --> 00:29:40.420
Me too.

00:29:53.830 --> 00:29:55.310
Oh, here it comes.

00:29:56.040 --> 00:29:57.020
Yeah.

00:30:21.700 --> 00:30:26.070
Summer vacation starts tomorrow,
but a vacation...

00:30:26.070 --> 00:30:29.640
Summer vacation starts tomorrow.
Tomorrow...

00:30:31.850 --> 00:30:33.580
Alright?
-Yes!

00:30:37.340 --> 00:30:41.130
Hey, everyone! Let's take
a picture before summer vacation!

00:30:41.130 --> 00:30:43.780
Gather in front of the blackboard!

00:30:43.780 --> 00:30:47.360
Three! Two! One!

00:30:51.890 --> 00:30:53.580
Yukari-chan!

00:30:53.580 --> 00:30:55.410
Do you have a moment?

00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:57.370
Hmm?

00:30:57.370 --> 00:30:58.940
It's something serious...

00:30:58.940 --> 00:31:03.360
Sanae-chan said she's going to start
track and field when entering high school.

00:31:03.360 --> 00:31:05.760
That's no big deal.

00:31:06.240 --> 00:31:08.120
What's so sad about that?

00:31:08.120 --> 00:31:11.660
The thing is...

00:31:12.540 --> 00:31:16.830
She's thinking about going to a
city high school for track and field.

00:31:28.640 --> 00:31:30.990
The three of us...

00:31:31.430 --> 00:31:34.990
...were a real success.
I wonder if that will change.

00:31:35.690 --> 00:31:38.560
Sooner or later it will change.

00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:41.960
It would be strange if things
would still be the same after 50 years.

00:31:42.650 --> 00:31:44.530
That's true, but...

00:32:05.760 --> 00:32:07.380
Hey, Nishikata!

00:32:07.380 --> 00:32:09.070
What are you thinking about?

00:32:09.510 --> 00:32:13.200
Something like, 
'I won't be able to see you tomorrow'?

00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:15.230
I was right!

00:32:17.310 --> 00:32:19.980
I was thinking the same thing.

00:32:19.980 --> 00:32:22.330
A reason for seeing you
during summer vacation.

00:32:25.820 --> 00:32:29.740
We can continue practicing how to
ride a bike together.

00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:32.870
Or we could study in the library.
But then we can't talk.

00:32:32.870 --> 00:32:37.620
You don't have to
make up reasons like that.

00:32:37.620 --> 00:32:42.130
I see... it would be nice if we 
could see each other without reason.

00:32:43.960 --> 00:32:47.730
Seeing each other without reason.
That means...

00:32:47.730 --> 00:32:49.690
...we are going...

00:32:49.690 --> 00:32:51.150
For example!

00:32:51.150 --> 00:32:53.360
For example?

00:32:55.680 --> 00:32:58.530
Doing the radio gymnastics every day.

00:32:58.530 --> 00:33:00.490
That was it?

00:33:14.470 --> 00:33:16.910
How cute!

00:33:22.380 --> 00:33:24.060
It's so fluffy!

00:33:24.060 --> 00:33:26.940
It's rare to see a cat that won't
run away from you, Nishikata.

00:33:26.940 --> 00:33:32.100
You are a good kitty!

00:33:39.310 --> 00:33:44.080
Ahh! So cute!

00:33:46.320 --> 00:33:50.290
There, there.

00:33:51.910 --> 00:33:54.570
Where might be the mother?

00:33:56.740 --> 00:33:59.260
Meow! Meow!

00:33:59.260 --> 00:34:01.510
Ms. cat-mother!

00:34:01.510 --> 00:34:04.520
Mom, where are you?

00:34:05.790 --> 00:34:07.650
Come out!

00:34:08.920 --> 00:34:11.010
Heeey!

00:34:13.010 --> 00:34:14.390
She's not here.

00:34:14.390 --> 00:34:16.430
I wonder if they've
lost track of each other.

00:34:16.430 --> 00:34:18.810
It's such a tiny little thing.

00:34:18.810 --> 00:34:20.620
Are you all alone?

00:34:21.690 --> 00:34:26.580
It would be nice if we could keep it
at home, but my mother is allergic to cats.

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:32.920
My dad got scratched when he was little,
so he said cats aren't allowed...

00:34:39.870 --> 00:34:43.680
Alright, Takagi-san!
Let's find an owner for this kitty!

00:34:43.680 --> 00:34:46.680
Yes!

00:34:47.130 --> 00:34:50.170
Until we find a new home,
I will take care of you here every day.

00:34:50.170 --> 00:34:50.900
Me too!

00:34:56.760 --> 00:35:00.270
Hey, hey, that tickles.

00:35:00.270 --> 00:35:02.890
Oh, it might be hungry.

00:35:02.890 --> 00:35:04.790
Oh, right.

00:35:04.790 --> 00:35:06.370
Takagi-san!

00:35:06.370 --> 00:35:09.770
There's a place I want to go with you.

00:35:16.530 --> 00:35:20.010
Oh, there's a customer coming!

00:35:20.010 --> 00:35:21.720
Yeees!

00:35:23.750 --> 00:35:27.210
Welcome!
-Ah, may I?

00:35:27.210 --> 00:35:30.380
Ms. Ota, the first customer in 100 years!

00:35:30.380 --> 00:35:32.760
Huh?
-Hey!

00:35:32.760 --> 00:35:35.400
I'm sorry, he is joking.
Come in!

00:35:35.400 --> 00:35:39.010
Come in! Come in!

00:35:39.010 --> 00:35:42.870
We found this kitty at the shrine just now.

00:35:42.870 --> 00:35:45.810
We think it's hungry.

00:35:47.060 --> 00:35:49.620
I've never seen such a little kitty before.

00:35:49.620 --> 00:35:52.730
We don't know what kind of food it needs.

00:35:52.730 --> 00:35:55.210
Could you tell us?
That's why we brought it here.

00:35:55.210 --> 00:35:56.920
I see.

00:35:57.860 --> 00:35:59.870
Let me see you for a moment.

00:35:59.870 --> 00:36:00.880
Yes!

00:36:01.660 --> 00:36:05.850
Good kitty... So cute!
Ah, she's a girl.

00:36:05.850 --> 00:36:07.430
Hey, don't eat it!

00:36:09.040 --> 00:36:12.750
Come on! I'm so sorry.
He is joking too much!

00:36:12.750 --> 00:36:15.220
I'm so sorry! He is joking too much!

00:36:15.220 --> 00:36:17.020
Katsuo! Be quiet for a moment!

00:36:17.020 --> 00:36:20.010
Ah, I'm Katsuo.
Nice to meet you!

00:36:21.260 --> 00:36:24.220
Mii!

00:36:25.060 --> 00:36:28.660
The teeth feel like
she was born about a month ago.

00:36:28.660 --> 00:36:31.020
A month...

00:36:31.020 --> 00:36:34.610
She's still slender, but healthy. 
She should be fine.

00:36:34.610 --> 00:36:37.240
Many of the girls are slender.

00:36:37.240 --> 00:36:39.160
So she's healthy.

00:36:39.160 --> 00:36:40.280
Yeah, don't worry.

00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:44.640
She might be able to eat food,
but first let's go with milk.

00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:48.600
This is milk for kittens.

00:36:49.670 --> 00:36:51.500
Why not regular milk?

00:36:51.500 --> 00:36:53.310
That's not good!

00:36:53.960 --> 00:36:57.720
Kittens can't digest it.
It will upset their stomach.

00:36:59.050 --> 00:37:00.990
Here, it's delicious!

00:37:09.620 --> 00:37:12.580
After all, you were hungry.

00:37:13.020 --> 00:37:14.540
That's a relief.

00:37:14.980 --> 00:37:18.070
She seems to like it.

00:37:18.070 --> 00:37:20.250
Delicious! Delicious!

00:37:25.630 --> 00:37:30.100
This one and this...
Okay, that will be 2300 Yen.

00:37:30.100 --> 00:37:32.500
Here.

00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:36.550
I never thought my 'teasing savings'
would come handy in a place like this.

00:37:36.550 --> 00:37:38.010
Teasing savings?

00:37:38.010 --> 00:37:40.340
Oh, no!
I said it out loud.

00:37:42.390 --> 00:37:44.550
You are a teasing-saver!

00:37:44.550 --> 00:37:46.570
I'm Nishikata!

00:37:48.530 --> 00:37:50.980
If she gets sick or something...

00:37:50.980 --> 00:37:52.810
...you can always bring her in.

00:37:52.810 --> 00:37:55.750
I can refer you to a veterinary hospital
that will take care of her right away.

00:37:55.750 --> 00:37:58.460
Okay!
-Come visit us again!

00:38:06.800 --> 00:38:09.010
Yukari-chan! Sanae-chan!

00:38:09.010 --> 00:38:10.100
Hmm?

00:38:11.710 --> 00:38:12.810
Ta-da!

00:38:13.880 --> 00:38:16.520
100 things I want to do
with you this summer!

00:38:18.510 --> 00:38:20.130
Come on! Come on!

00:38:21.970 --> 00:38:23.980
What do you want to do?

00:38:23.980 --> 00:38:26.950
Really? A hundred of them?
-Of course!

00:38:27.510 --> 00:38:32.020
We have to do it soon.
We only have one summer in third grade.

00:38:32.020 --> 00:38:35.410
Right? Right?
Come on! Come on!

00:38:37.230 --> 00:38:39.250
Watermelon.

00:38:41.110 --> 00:38:43.460
I want to spit watermelon seeds.

00:38:43.460 --> 00:38:45.800
Yes! Yes!

00:38:46.410 --> 00:38:48.870
I'd like to find a
winning ice cream stick.

00:38:48.870 --> 00:38:50.410
Yes, that's good!

00:38:50.410 --> 00:38:53.760
But this summer...
It's okay to get serious!

00:38:56.500 --> 00:39:00.510
I want to make a
cicada shell into a brooch.

00:39:00.510 --> 00:39:03.480
Yes! Yes!
You too, Yukari-chan!

00:39:04.180 --> 00:39:07.170
Me?
-Yes!

00:39:08.970 --> 00:39:13.940
Well, yeah...
Personally, I'd like to experience love.

00:39:13.940 --> 00:39:17.610
Or I'd rather want to talk about love.

00:39:17.610 --> 00:39:21.230
A sleepover with the three of us.
And we talk about love till the morning.

00:39:21.230 --> 00:39:27.260
It's our youth after all.
I would adore that.

00:39:27.260 --> 00:39:29.910
I want to tie up somen inside my mouth.

00:39:29.910 --> 00:39:33.000
Good! Good!

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:34.220
Erm...

00:39:34.220 --> 00:39:35.670
Looking at the stars...

00:39:35.670 --> 00:39:38.350
Listen to me for a second!

00:39:40.310 --> 00:39:45.130
Sorry. Until we find your new home,
this will be your home.

00:39:45.130 --> 00:39:46.480
Are you alright?

00:39:48.430 --> 00:39:50.140
Good kitty!

00:39:50.860 --> 00:39:54.180
I hope you like it, Shiro.

00:39:54.180 --> 00:39:57.190
Shiro?
-Ah, Shiro...

00:39:58.100 --> 00:40:00.160
That's her name?

00:40:00.160 --> 00:40:02.900
Yes! She's pure white. Shiro!

00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:04.540
Shiro-chan!

00:40:07.500 --> 00:40:09.720
No answer?

00:40:09.720 --> 00:40:12.430
That's right, Takagi-san!
Let's have a contest.

00:40:12.430 --> 00:40:15.040
It's a naming contest!

00:40:15.040 --> 00:40:16.890
Come up with a name
and try calling her.

00:40:17.330 --> 00:40:20.350
You win if she answers with a 'Mii'.

00:40:25.880 --> 00:40:26.770
Sounds good!

00:40:29.970 --> 00:40:31.240
Hmm...

00:40:31.240 --> 00:40:35.700
'Gorogoro' sounds a bit too boyish.

00:40:36.270 --> 00:40:38.560
She always says 'Mii Mii'...

00:40:38.560 --> 00:40:41.660
But if she's grown up,
it will be 'Meow Meow'.

00:40:44.030 --> 00:40:47.110
Oh! I've got an amazing idea!

00:40:47.110 --> 00:40:49.670
I'm good! 
I feel like I can only win!

00:40:50.410 --> 00:40:52.780
Takagi-san, I just had an idea.

00:40:52.780 --> 00:40:55.680
Oh, that was fast!
You can go first!

00:41:01.210 --> 00:41:02.420
Yuki!

00:41:04.800 --> 00:41:05.270
Yuki!

00:41:11.640 --> 00:41:14.640
Yuki? Like the falling snow?

00:41:14.640 --> 00:41:16.160
Well, yeah...

00:41:16.160 --> 00:41:18.620
That's a good name.
It's cute.

00:41:19.140 --> 00:41:21.440
Yeah, but...

00:41:21.440 --> 00:41:23.400
...no answer.

00:41:23.400 --> 00:41:25.400
But why?

00:41:26.990 --> 00:41:29.450
Snow is so white and beautiful.

00:41:29.450 --> 00:41:32.050
It would be perfect for you.
That's why I chose Yuki.

00:41:35.330 --> 00:41:39.160
We can't help it, Nishikata.
She is still only one month old.

00:41:39.160 --> 00:41:42.980
She has never seen or heard
of snow, right?

00:41:42.980 --> 00:41:48.270
That's true...
You don't know how snow looks like yet.

00:41:48.270 --> 00:41:51.860
I wonder how big you will
be when it's winter...

00:41:51.860 --> 00:41:54.240
...and you see your first snow.

00:41:57.020 --> 00:41:59.430
So, then it's my turn.

00:41:59.430 --> 00:42:00.910
'Mii'

00:42:00.910 --> 00:42:04.660
Takagi-san, that's the name
I already rejected.

00:42:05.770 --> 00:42:06.620
'Mii-chan'

00:42:08.440 --> 00:42:11.110
'Mii', 'Mii-chan'

00:42:11.110 --> 00:42:12.780
'Mii', 'Mii-chan'

00:42:12.780 --> 00:42:14.570
Stop it, Takagi-san!

00:42:14.570 --> 00:42:17.700
If you call her so many times
she won't answer you.

00:42:17.700 --> 00:42:21.390
Did you call her 'Mii-chan' because
she's always saying 'Mii Mii'?

00:42:21.830 --> 00:42:23.350
Yes, that's right!

00:42:23.920 --> 00:42:28.210
You know what, Takagi-san?
She will only do that as a kitten.

00:42:28.210 --> 00:42:31.840
When she's grown up,
it will be 'Meow'.

00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:34.510
Is this okay?
With a name like that?

00:42:34.510 --> 00:42:36.490
Yes!

00:42:37.100 --> 00:42:39.450
I would want to remember...

00:42:39.450 --> 00:42:41.380
...how she was saying 'Mii Mii'.

00:42:57.130 --> 00:43:00.910
Hey, hey. You startled me,
running off like that.

00:43:00.910 --> 00:43:02.460
I'm glad she's fine...

00:43:02.460 --> 00:43:05.040
...but it could be dangerous if
she were to run onto a road.

00:43:05.040 --> 00:43:06.460
Right!

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:09.060
You like flowers?

00:43:11.510 --> 00:43:12.610
Hana!

00:43:12.610 --> 00:43:14.820
Hana!
Because she likes flowers!

00:43:14.820 --> 00:43:17.280
Yes! Hana!

00:43:21.310 --> 00:43:23.430
Hana!

00:43:23.430 --> 00:43:26.160
Hana!

00:43:28.440 --> 00:43:32.190
That tickles!

00:43:32.190 --> 00:43:33.950
Hana!

00:44:01.110 --> 00:44:03.640
Takagi-san, good morning!

00:44:04.560 --> 00:44:05.910
Good morning, Nishikata!

00:44:05.910 --> 00:44:06.910
How's Hana?

00:44:07.560 --> 00:44:10.870
She drank some milk and went to the toilet.
Then she fell asleep.

00:44:10.870 --> 00:44:13.150
Ah, sorry!

00:44:14.320 --> 00:44:15.900
I see, I see...

00:44:15.900 --> 00:44:19.620
She was in the house when I got here.

00:44:19.620 --> 00:44:24.050
I see, I see...
Good kitty!

00:44:24.790 --> 00:44:26.970
Hana! Hana-chan!

00:44:28.620 --> 00:44:31.840
Hana! Haana-chan!

00:44:35.010 --> 00:44:36.150
Right, Takagi-san!

00:44:38.680 --> 00:44:42.530
Look at this!
Let's make fliers to find a foster parent!

00:44:42.530 --> 00:44:44.390
Let's put them at various spots!

00:44:44.390 --> 00:44:46.990
At shops and at the veterinary hospital...

00:44:52.060 --> 00:44:55.170
Did I say something funny?

00:44:55.170 --> 00:44:56.380
No...

00:44:58.200 --> 00:45:00.300
You see...

00:45:00.740 --> 00:45:03.760
We thought of the same thing!

00:45:03.760 --> 00:45:08.930
Anyone could have thought of that.

00:45:08.930 --> 00:45:12.430
Should we make them together?

00:45:27.520 --> 00:45:31.700
<i>♪ Hamabou flowers. ♪</i>

00:45:32.480 --> 00:45:37.400
<i>♪ Swaying innocently. ♪</i>

00:45:37.400 --> 00:45:42.370
<i>♪ Lively colors. ♪</i>

00:45:42.370 --> 00:45:46.300
<i>♪ Our usual walkway. ♪</i>

00:45:47.290 --> 00:45:51.420
<i>♪ A little hide-and-seek... ♪</i>

00:45:51.970 --> 00:45:57.050
<i>♪ ...just behind you. ♪</i>

00:45:57.050 --> 00:46:02.130
<i>♪ I have a feeling... ♪</i>

00:46:02.130 --> 00:46:05.990
<i>♪ ...you'll find me soon. ♪</i>

00:46:07.240 --> 00:46:12.060
<i>♪ In the sunshine, ♪</i>

00:46:12.060 --> 00:46:16.750
<i>♪ we'll always be... ♪</i>

00:46:16.750 --> 00:46:21.990
<i>♪ ...chasing each other, round and round. ♪</i>

00:46:21.990 --> 00:46:26.950
<i>♪ Everyday, like marbles. ♪</i>

00:46:26.950 --> 00:46:39.020
<i>♪ I wonder what lies beyond ♪
♪ that gentle slope. ♪</i>

00:46:46.720 --> 00:46:55.720
<i>♪ Spread out the story like a map. ♪</i>

00:46:56.540 --> 00:47:04.610
<i>♪ We're looking for the treasure together. ♪</i>

00:47:06.490 --> 00:47:11.050
<i>♪ Something as elusive as the sun... ♪</i>

00:47:11.050 --> 00:47:16.420
<i>♪ ...shining through the trees. ♪</i>

00:47:16.420 --> 00:47:21.340
<i>♪ Chasing each other, round and round. ♪</i>

00:47:21.340 --> 00:47:25.570
<i>♪ The sky, reflecting in a marble... ♪</i>

00:47:26.220 --> 00:47:30.600
<i>♪ ...locking up everything inside. ♪</i>

00:47:30.600 --> 00:47:39.150
<i>♪ Our summer memories. ♪</i>

00:47:42.080 --> 00:47:46.410
Wow, Hana!
You're good at this!

00:47:46.410 --> 00:47:48.170
Got any replies, Nishikata?

00:47:50.080 --> 00:47:52.580
No, not yet...

00:47:52.580 --> 00:47:53.830
I see...

00:47:55.760 --> 00:48:00.800
It's apparently not easy
to find a foster parent.

00:48:02.130 --> 00:48:04.380
It will be alright!

00:48:04.380 --> 00:48:07.530
Because Hana is cute!

00:48:38.330 --> 00:48:46.730
<i>♪ I don't know why the clock ♪
♪ keeps ticking on days I spend with you. ♪</i>

00:48:47.590 --> 00:48:55.810
<i>♪ Like it's broken. Time is ticking away. ♪</i>

00:49:02.730 --> 00:49:12.700
<i>♪ Until we reach the end ♪
♪ of the gently sloping road... ♪</i>

00:49:12.700 --> 00:49:22.540
<i>♪ ...we'll never change, ♪
♪ we'll innocently play around. ♪</i>

00:49:22.540 --> 00:49:27.550
<i>♪ Chasing each other, round and round. ♪</i>

00:49:27.550 --> 00:49:32.430
<i>♪ The scenery, reflecting in a marble... ♪</i>

00:49:32.430 --> 00:49:36.110
<i>♪ ...locking up everything inside. ♪</i>

00:49:36.810 --> 00:49:43.270
<i>♪ To always be remembered. ♪</i>

00:49:43.270 --> 00:49:50.070
<i>♪ To always be remembered. ♪</i>

00:50:08.630 --> 00:50:12.730
Hana, how about a contest?
We'll play whack-a-mole.

00:50:13.220 --> 00:50:16.100
You've built something impressive again!
-Well...

00:50:16.100 --> 00:50:19.310
If Hana can't beat me in
one minute, I win.

00:50:19.310 --> 00:50:22.020
If Hana manages to hit me once,
she wins.

00:50:22.020 --> 00:50:23.620
She can win a special treat.

00:50:24.060 --> 00:50:25.870
And you can treat me to a drink!

00:50:26.320 --> 00:50:29.940
Sounds good!
Eh! For you too, Takagi-san?

00:50:29.940 --> 00:50:31.540
Yeah!

00:50:31.540 --> 00:50:34.510
He's going to treat me.
Do your best​!

00:50:35.070 --> 00:50:38.990
Have a good look,
Hana and Takagi-san!

00:50:38.990 --> 00:50:40.700
Okay, here we go!

00:50:43.330 --> 00:50:46.880
What do you think of my
nimble mole handling skills?

00:50:46.880 --> 00:50:50.270
But she's so cute!
Hana...

00:50:50.880 --> 00:50:53.300
Hmm, there aren't any moles.

00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:54.230
Stop meddling!

00:50:54.800 --> 00:50:57.070
Its alright.
The victory will be mine!

00:50:58.240 --> 00:50:59.700
That Nishikata is cute!

00:51:05.330 --> 00:51:07.290
Wow! That's amazing, Hana!

00:51:07.290 --> 00:51:08.870
One more round!

00:51:11.790 --> 00:51:16.530
We get double the treats!

00:51:17.260 --> 00:51:20.700
Damn you, Hana and Takagi-san!

00:51:20.700 --> 00:51:22.470
Hey, Nishikata?
-Hmm?

00:51:24.250 --> 00:51:26.890
I think I will ask again...

00:51:28.710 --> 00:51:31.690
... so I can take Hana home.

00:51:31.690 --> 00:51:34.900
That's great!

00:51:34.900 --> 00:51:39.320
I think that's wonderful!
Then Hana can always stay with us.

00:51:40.530 --> 00:51:46.490
Maybe I can come visit?
If that's okay.

00:51:46.940 --> 00:51:48.650
Me?

00:51:48.650 --> 00:51:51.420
No!
I mean Hana, obviously...

00:51:51.860 --> 00:51:55.960
What? Nishikata doesn't
want to visit me.

00:51:55.960 --> 00:51:57.710
I didn't say that!

00:52:00.830 --> 00:52:03.910
Ah, come on!

00:52:11.710 --> 00:52:14.050
I haven't blown soap bubbles in ages.

00:52:14.050 --> 00:52:14.770
Yeah.

00:52:15.260 --> 00:52:17.550
So, what's next?

00:52:17.550 --> 00:52:18.550
Hmm?

00:52:24.890 --> 00:52:25.930
Oh...

00:52:27.600 --> 00:52:29.190
I think we're done.

00:52:29.190 --> 00:52:33.920
Eh, why? You didn't say that?

00:52:34.360 --> 00:52:36.040
Yes, but...

00:52:36.820 --> 00:52:39.320
Once you have decided,
finish what you've started.

00:52:39.320 --> 00:52:41.260
That's real sportsmanship!

00:52:42.690 --> 00:52:44.700
It's because...

00:52:44.700 --> 00:52:49.080
If we did all 100 of them,
it would be the end of our summer.

00:52:50.540 --> 00:52:52.920
I don't want it to end.

00:52:52.920 --> 00:52:56.110
I want it to go on forever.

00:52:56.110 --> 00:53:01.390
Heeey!

00:53:09.350 --> 00:53:11.770
Heeey!

00:53:12.820 --> 00:53:15.250
Heeey!

00:53:15.250 --> 00:53:18.490
Heeey!

00:53:19.490 --> 00:53:21.620
Heeey!

00:53:21.620 --> 00:53:23.950
Heeey!

00:54:14.460 --> 00:54:16.090
I wonder how Hana is doing...

00:54:16.090 --> 00:54:17.440
Ota-san!

00:54:17.440 --> 00:54:18.900
Hello!

00:54:18.900 --> 00:54:22.010
Hello!
Is Hana still healthy?

00:54:22.010 --> 00:54:23.110
Healthy?

00:54:23.550 --> 00:54:24.820
Yes, absolutely!

00:54:24.820 --> 00:54:28.910
Actually, thanks to you,
we will be able to keep her at our house!

00:54:30.230 --> 00:54:32.270
We wanted to let you know first!

00:54:32.270 --> 00:54:35.150
Woah, congratulations!

00:54:35.150 --> 00:54:37.870
Hey, hey! You're as loud as a bomb!

00:54:37.870 --> 00:54:41.320
Ah, Sorry!
I'm so happy!

00:54:41.320 --> 00:54:43.200
I've been thinking about it a lot.

00:54:43.200 --> 00:54:46.330
It's about time for Hana-chan
to find a real home.

00:54:46.330 --> 00:54:47.470
That’s great!

00:54:48.120 --> 00:54:49.390
Yeah!

00:54:51.100 --> 00:54:55.130
I'll give you something to celebrate.
Choose a present you like.

00:54:55.130 --> 00:54:57.190
Waah!
-Thank You!

00:54:58.050 --> 00:54:59.400
Let's see which one
suits her best.

00:54:59.400 --> 00:55:04.110
That's right.
Anything would look good on her.

00:55:04.110 --> 00:55:07.240
What would be the best...

00:55:08.060 --> 00:55:09.320
Look, this!

00:55:09.320 --> 00:55:12.700
Hana's favorite flowers!

00:55:12.700 --> 00:55:15.190
Right?
-Hana, you will be happy!

00:55:15.190 --> 00:55:17.270
Yes!

00:55:17.270 --> 00:55:19.110
What a nice couple!

00:55:19.110 --> 00:55:20.540
Shush!
-Ah!

00:55:21.070 --> 00:55:22.710
Hana, we have a present!

00:55:23.990 --> 00:55:25.420
Hana!

00:55:26.490 --> 00:55:27.660
Hmm?

00:55:28.780 --> 00:55:29.880
Hana?

00:55:32.410 --> 00:55:35.750
She's probably chasing
butterflies again.

00:55:38.090 --> 00:55:39.520
Hana!

00:55:39.520 --> 00:55:44.230
At Takagi-san's home
you can't be a rascal anymore.

00:55:44.840 --> 00:55:46.550
Hana!

00:55:46.550 --> 00:55:47.760
Hana!

00:55:49.140 --> 00:55:51.180
Hana!

00:55:51.180 --> 00:55:52.160
Hana!

00:56:14.160 --> 00:56:16.120
Did she go for a walk?

00:56:16.120 --> 00:56:17.960
What if she suddenly ran onto the street...

00:56:23.340 --> 00:56:25.920
I'll look downstairs at our meeting place.

00:56:25.920 --> 00:56:28.220
I'll look at the top of the hill.

00:56:28.220 --> 00:56:29.490
Mommy, look at this!

00:56:29.970 --> 00:56:30.970
What is it?

00:56:30.970 --> 00:56:33.270
Brother found a cat!

00:56:33.270 --> 00:56:34.910
Oh my!

00:56:35.350 --> 00:56:38.080
It was on the stairs of the shrine.

00:56:38.080 --> 00:56:40.730
So cute!
Can we keep it?

00:56:40.730 --> 00:56:42.710
Eh?
-Okay?

00:56:42.710 --> 00:56:45.490
I'll talk to them!

00:56:45.490 --> 00:56:48.840
She looks just like our Nana-chan,
who is in heaven now.

00:56:48.840 --> 00:56:52.800
So white and fluffy.
The round eyes are the same!

00:56:52.800 --> 00:56:55.410
She looks just like Nana-chan.

00:56:58.220 --> 00:57:02.960
Nana-chan must have returned to us.

00:57:02.960 --> 00:57:06.090
That must be it!
-That's right, Nana-chan!

00:57:07.170 --> 00:57:07.690
See!

00:57:08.380 --> 00:57:11.150
That's right.
-Welcome home, Nana-chan!

00:57:13.060 --> 00:57:14.320
Nana!

00:57:14.320 --> 00:57:17.600
Okay!
We'll be together again.

00:57:18.890 --> 00:57:21.790
I'm glad we kept Nana-chan's toys!

00:57:21.790 --> 00:57:25.250
Let's play again, Nana!

00:57:26.750 --> 00:57:30.200
We will always stay together.

00:58:48.650 --> 00:58:49.630
I'm glad...

00:58:56.740 --> 00:58:58.220
That girl.

00:58:59.790 --> 00:59:02.410
She looked happy.

00:59:04.670 --> 00:59:07.090
I'm sure...

00:59:08.550 --> 00:59:11.940
...she will be happy forever.

00:59:24.080 --> 00:59:29.360
Hana will be happy. I know it.

00:59:30.480 --> 00:59:32.500
You too, Takagi-san.

00:59:33.820 --> 00:59:35.460
Takagi-san, you will be happy.

00:59:39.700 --> 00:59:43.210
I will make you happy, Takagi-san!

00:59:54.880 --> 00:59:57.930
Definitely. Always.

00:59:57.930 --> 00:59:59.140
Always.

01:00:18.820 --> 01:00:20.740
Rock! Paper! Scissors!

01:00:20.740 --> 01:00:23.750
PA I NA TSU PU RU
(Pineapple)

01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:26.750
Rock! Paper!...

01:00:32.170 --> 01:00:33.840
Miisuke!

01:00:38.690 --> 01:00:41.300
Rock! Paper! Scissors!

01:00:41.300 --> 01:00:43.850
No scissors today...
So it's a paper strategy?

01:00:43.850 --> 01:00:45.910
Well...

01:00:54.630 --> 01:00:57.590
Oh, the couple from last year!

01:00:58.030 --> 01:01:00.920
Don't get lost this year.
-Yes...

01:01:01.450 --> 01:01:06.540
Your face is as red as an apple!
Just kidding!

01:01:09.970 --> 01:01:12.290
That’s wonderful,
they're doing well.

01:01:12.290 --> 01:01:13.710
What's the matter?​

01:01:13.710 --> 01:01:15.380
Ah, sorry!

01:01:19.430 --> 01:01:22.530
Sanae, I thought you were going to
a high school in the city.

01:01:22.530 --> 01:01:23.760
Yeah.

01:01:23.760 --> 01:01:26.740
You wanted to take
track and field seriously.

01:01:26.740 --> 01:01:29.900
My advisor recommended me to do it.

01:01:29.900 --> 01:01:32.960
But I can do it seriously at a
high school on the island.

01:01:32.960 --> 01:01:34.270
Ah!

01:01:39.530 --> 01:01:42.010
That’s great!

01:01:44.200 --> 01:01:48.220
So it was a false alarm.

01:01:50.000 --> 01:01:52.290
The three of us will be
together from now on.

01:01:52.290 --> 01:01:57.810
There are 100 things I want to do.
...1000... ...100 million...

01:01:57.810 --> 01:01:59.840
Well, let's see...

01:01:59.840 --> 01:02:03.320
Okay, let's start with the ring toss!

01:02:03.320 --> 01:02:06.860
Yes! Throw it as good as you can!

01:02:11.900 --> 01:02:13.980
That's nice!

01:02:13.980 --> 01:02:15.120
Okay, one more.

01:02:17.730 --> 01:02:20.530
Isn't this getting too serious?

01:02:20.530 --> 01:02:23.070
Hehehe, I became hooked.

01:02:23.070 --> 01:02:26.050
Alright, let's shoot the firework next!

01:02:26.740 --> 01:02:31.600
There's a secret spot with
a first class seat!

01:02:32.330 --> 01:02:33.810
Takao!
-Eh?

01:02:34.250 --> 01:02:36.460
Let's go up.
-Eh?

01:02:36.460 --> 01:02:40.400
We're shooting from higher up.
Right?

01:02:40.400 --> 01:02:43.010
Eh?...

01:02:45.050 --> 01:02:47.600
Oh! Yeah, right!

01:02:50.480 --> 01:02:52.690
Let's go!
-Okay!

01:02:58.110 --> 01:03:00.420
Shall we go?
-Yes!

01:03:17.130 --> 01:03:20.590
It really is a first class seat!

01:03:20.590 --> 01:03:21.630
Yes!

01:03:31.390 --> 01:03:34.020
Hey, Nishikata!
-Hmm?

01:03:35.520 --> 01:03:38.550
I'll make you happy too, Nishikata!

01:03:44.320 --> 01:03:45.360
Okay!

01:04:23.690 --> 01:04:29.530
<i>♪ Glowing sweat, ♪
♪ T-shirts, and the love I found. ♪</i>

01:04:29.530 --> 01:04:35.410
<i>♪ You shine brighter ♪
♪ than anyone else. ♪</i>

01:04:35.410 --> 01:04:40.500
<i>♪ I discovered my first love. ♪</i>

01:04:41.140 --> 01:04:47.090
<i>♪ A new journey begins. ♪</i>

01:04:47.090 --> 01:04:52.930
<i>♪ After the rain, ♪
♪ a whimsical blue breeze. ♪</i>

01:04:52.930 --> 01:04:58.810
<i>♪ The intense sunshine. ♪
♪ Someday I will overtake. ♪</i>

01:04:58.810 --> 01:05:03.810
<i>♪ The color of love, that ♪
♪ I will draw from now on... ♪</i>

01:05:04.690 --> 01:05:10.530
<i>♪ ...will be on the first page. ♪</i>

01:05:10.530 --> 01:05:16.410
<i>♪ Like in a ♪
♪ fortune-telling magazine. ♪</i>

01:05:16.410 --> 01:05:22.420
<i>♪ Let's align our future ♪
♪ with two stars. ♪</i>

01:05:22.420 --> 01:05:28.090
<i>♪ My scarred heart... ♪</i>

01:05:28.090 --> 01:05:35.520
<i>♪ ...healed by your kindness. ♪</i>

01:05:36.470 --> 01:05:42.770
<i>♪ Before I knew it, ♪
♪ my empty heart was filled. ♪</i>

01:05:42.770 --> 01:05:48.070
<i>♪ A casual gesture at ♪
♪ an unexpected moment. ♪</i>

01:05:48.070 --> 01:05:54.580
<i>♪ Someday, when you talk ♪
♪ about your dreams... ♪</i>

01:05:54.580 --> 01:05:59.100
<i>♪ I want to gaze at your♪
♪ face and smile. ♪</i>

01:06:12.050 --> 01:06:17.810
<i>♪ When you protect ♪
♪ something precious... ♪</i>

01:06:17.810 --> 01:06:23.690
<i>♪ ...the first step is courage. ♪</i>

01:06:23.690 --> 01:06:29.570
<i>♪ It's always just a ♪
♪ roundabout way, ♪</i>

01:06:29.570 --> 01:06:35.530
<i>♪ ...if you run away ♪
♪ from being hurt. ♪</i>

01:06:35.530 --> 01:06:41.290
<i>♪ I'm lost inside ♪
♪ my heart... ♪</i>

01:06:41.290 --> 01:06:47.060
<i>♪ ...with a habit to be tough, ♪
♪ that has lost its place. ♪</i>

01:06:47.060 --> 01:06:52.970
<i>♪ Tears well up ♪
♪ more than words... ♪</i>

01:06:52.970 --> 01:06:58.520
<i>♪ ...when I learned of your ♪
♪ feelings for the first time. ♪</i>

01:06:58.520 --> 01:07:04.730
<i>♪ Let's walk one step at a time ♪
♪ with slightly different feet. ♪</i>

01:07:04.730 --> 01:07:10.360
<i>♪ The road we walk together ♪
♪ is a bumpy one. ♪</i>

01:07:10.360 --> 01:07:15.840
<i>♪ A small commitment to write ♪
♪ on a folded white map. ♪</i>

01:07:16.370 --> 01:07:22.210
<i>♪ I'm telling you honestly. ♪</i>

01:07:46.350 --> 01:07:52.280
<i>♪ You can hear the melody of ♪
♪ two people close to your ear. ♪</i>

01:07:52.280 --> 01:07:58.120
<i>♪ Hold back the ♪
♪ gushing tears. ♪</i>

01:07:58.120 --> 01:08:03.200
<i>♪ I'll tell you with ♪
♪ simple words. ♪</i>

01:08:03.200 --> 01:08:10.460
<i>♪ From now on, ♪
♪ we'll always be together. ♪</i>

01:08:11.460 --> 01:08:17.970
<i>♪ This uncontrollable feeling, ♪
♪ coming from the midnight sky. ♪</i>

01:08:17.970 --> 01:08:22.990
<i>♪ Pouring down ♪
♪ as shining drops. ♪</i>

01:08:22.990 --> 01:08:29.520
<i>♪ I've realized. A gentle breeze ♪
♪ is touching my heart. ♪</i>

01:08:29.520 --> 01:08:35.360
<i>♪ The door to ♪
♪ tomorrow opens softly. ♪</i>

01:08:40.700 --> 01:08:47.170
<i>♪ Words transcend time ♪
♪ and pierce through eternity ♪</i>

01:08:47.170 --> 01:08:51.770
<i>♪ Passing through ♪
♪ many seasons. ♪</i>

01:08:52.460 --> 01:08:58.840
<i>♪ We finally arrive at our place ♪
♪ after a long journey. ♪</i>

01:08:58.840 --> 01:09:04.720
<i>♪ Let's nurture the ♪
♪ love we swore. ♪</i>

01:10:24.300 --> 01:10:28.680
Tomose! Tomose!

01:10:28.680 --> 01:10:32.870
Tomose! Tomose!

01:10:32.870 --> 01:10:37.070
Tomose! Tomose!

01:10:37.070 --> 01:10:39.380
Hmm?

01:10:41.530 --> 01:10:42.880
Ah?

01:10:45.090 --> 01:10:47.910
Let's follow that kid.

01:10:47.910 --> 01:10:51.180
That kid? Chi?

01:10:54.640 --> 01:10:56.640
Ah, it went out.

01:10:56.640 --> 01:10:59.100
Stay by my side.
We'll get some light.

01:10:59.100 --> 01:11:01.110
Okaasan? Chi?

01:11:02.010 --> 01:11:03.110
Ah!

01:11:16.900 --> 01:11:21.380
Wow! Fireflies!
How beautiful!

01:11:29.340 --> 01:11:33.500
Hmm, where is he?

01:11:33.500 --> 01:11:34.310
Who?

01:11:34.310 --> 01:11:37.770
Somebody called me
over here.

01:11:37.770 --> 01:11:41.050
Might have been Kaboso, the Yokai.

01:11:41.050 --> 01:11:42.670
Ah, that's...
-Waa!

01:11:42.670 --> 01:11:45.180
Kaboso! Kaboso!

01:11:45.180 --> 01:11:47.280
Dad, are you scared?

01:11:47.280 --> 01:11:51.890
I'm not scared.
Because Kaboso is friends with me.

01:11:51.890 --> 01:11:53.180
Really?

01:11:53.180 --> 01:11:56.520
Geez!
You two are teasing me again!

01:12:01.070 --> 01:12:04.070
I wish I could have shown
this to Saku-chan.

01:12:05.530 --> 01:12:08.780
I hope Saku-chan is good
while watching our home.

01:12:25.010 --> 01:12:26.380
We're home!

